So yeah,
so now we're going to talk a little bit

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8708-1
01:12:05.968 --> 01:12:09.147
about GPU history and where GPUs came
from.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8745-0
01:12:10.347 --> 01:12:15.192
So I say early,
they were quietly leading a parallel life,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8745-1
01:12:15.192 --> 01:12:20.448
parallel to GPU compute,
which wasn't what they originally were

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8745-2
01:12:20.448 --> 01:12:25.046
designed to do.
What they were designed to do was built

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8745-3
01:12:25.046 --> 01:12:28.987
into the name,
their graphics processing units.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8777-0
01:12:29.387 --> 01:12:35.846
and they were specifically designed
because in graphics processing with an

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8777-1
01:12:35.846 --> 01:12:42.304
image, you have a whole bunch of pixels,
right? And for a lot of purposes,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8777-2
01:12:42.304 --> 01:12:47.987
and there's a couple of different stages
in the graphics process.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8813-0
01:12:48.507 --> 01:12:54.506
rendering pipeline that are kind of what
we call embarrassingly parallel,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8813-1
01:12:54.506 --> 01:12:58.316
where they're kind of independent,
each pixel,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8813-2
01:12:58.316 --> 01:13:03.586
and when you're dealing with a 3D mesh
representation like this,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8813-3
01:13:03.586 --> 01:13:06.747
which is how objects in 3D graphics are

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8845-0
01:13:06.827 --> 01:13:11.734
represented,
they basically are modeled with a meshes,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8845-1
01:13:11.734 --> 01:13:16.106
polygonal,
triagonal meshes of various different

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8845-2
01:13:16.106 --> 01:13:20.656
complexities and densities depending on,
you know,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8845-3
01:13:20.656 --> 01:13:26.187
the object and the level of detail that
you want. But then...

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8856-0
01:13:26.347 --> 01:13:31.888
They get, um, you know,
each they get overlaid with these

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8856-1
01:13:31.888 --> 01:13:32.747
textures.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8891-0
01:13:34.067 --> 01:13:39.268
is 1 frequent way that it's done that
allows you to go from something that

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8891-1
01:13:39.268 --> 01:13:44.469
looks like this wireframe mesh to
something that looks like an actual real

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8891-2
01:13:44.469 --> 01:13:49.947
object with reflections and metallic
surfaces and lighting and all that stuff.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8904-0
01:13:51.787 --> 01:13:57.847
So there's just multiple stages of the
graphics rendering process,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8904-1
01:13:57.847 --> 01:14:00.107
each individual triangle.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8947-0
01:14:01.867 --> 01:14:06.332
and it is modeled is represented by a set
of vertices,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8947-1
01:14:06.332 --> 01:14:10.148
and so you have this massive grid of
vertices,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8947-2
01:14:10.148 --> 01:14:15.587
and then you have these like discrete
primitives called triangles,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8947-3
01:14:15.587 --> 01:14:21.107
and so they can be all processed kind of
in parallel independently.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8950-0
01:14:21.787 --> 01:14:24.027
So the idea was to build these.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8976-0
01:14:25.747 --> 01:14:32.317
processing devices which were
specifically designed to take in a grid

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/8976-1
01:14:32.317 --> 01:14:40.107
of triangles and then do the appropriate
processing that needs to be done on that.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9001-0
01:14:42.747 --> 01:14:48.347
That stage of the rendering process is
called vertex processing,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9001-1
01:14:48.347 --> 01:14:54.292
and then later on when those,
when you try to kind of project the 3D

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9001-2
01:14:54.292 --> 01:14:56.187
scene into a 2D image.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9044-0
01:14:58.667 --> 01:15:02.150
then you're dealing with pixels. So,
you know,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9044-1
01:15:02.150 --> 01:15:07.040
a typical image today may have millions,
many millions of pixels,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9044-2
01:15:07.040 --> 01:15:13.264
and each one of those pixels can be also
processed independently to a large extent.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9044-3
01:15:13.264 --> 01:15:18.747
And so there's this pixel processing
engine and vertex processing engines

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9075-0
01:15:19.027 --> 01:15:23.923
And in the early days of GPUs,
it was all like hard-coded,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9075-1
01:15:23.923 --> 01:15:28.487
it wasn't hard-coded,
but it was literally hard-wired,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9075-2
01:15:28.487 --> 01:15:33.964
fixed function units that would
specifically process vertices and

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9075-3
01:15:33.964 --> 01:15:37.947
specifically process fragment,
pixel fragments.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9084-0
01:15:40.907 --> 01:15:44.267
And it was designed just to allow you to
do 3D graphics really fast.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9094-0
01:15:45.627 --> 01:15:48.728
Which is great,
and then you know back in the early days

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9094-1
01:15:48.728 --> 01:15:49.707
of like the early.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9101-0
01:15:52.027 --> 01:15:55.467
Early GPU, early 3D graphics cards.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9119-0
01:15:56.907 --> 01:16:04.107
1990s were when they were first starting
to really come out with the basic fixed

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9119-1
01:16:04.107 --> 01:16:06.507
function 3D graphics cards.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9154-0
01:16:09.227 --> 01:16:14.189
They get, you know,
it was a game changer because we went

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9154-1
01:16:14.189 --> 01:16:19.664
from crappy, you know,
like Atari style graphics to actual like

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9154-2
01:16:19.664 --> 01:16:25.738
real time 3D representations.
They were still limited compared to what

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9154-3
01:16:25.738 --> 01:16:29.587
we can do today, but it was still like a..
.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9156-0
01:16:30.067 --> 01:16:31.067
a game changer.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9161-0
01:16:33.787 --> 01:16:36.747
And that was the very beginning of.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9177-0
01:16:38.187 --> 01:16:43.787
why people started to have like multiple
parallel cores that were on a device and

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9177-1
01:16:43.787 --> 01:16:46.587
why they were called graphics processing.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9189-0
01:16:47.867 --> 01:16:53.067
units and this is this graphics
processing pipeline that I was mentioning.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9232-0
01:16:54.347 --> 01:17:00.692
There's a series of stages that goes
through to create your output pixel image

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9232-1
01:17:00.692 --> 01:17:05.270
representation,
starting from an input collection of all

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9232-2
01:17:05.270 --> 01:17:09.688
these vertices.
Like you can imagine each one of these

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9232-3
01:17:09.688 --> 01:17:14.667
vertices is a 3D value in space,
and then they get connected.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9285-0
01:17:16.107 --> 01:17:20.380
So there's all these like vertex
generation, vertex processing,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9285-1
01:17:20.380 --> 01:17:24.920
and then from there you have to go to
convert those into, you know,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9285-2
01:17:24.920 --> 01:17:28.725
various different,
converting it to a raster grid for an

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9285-3
01:17:28.725 --> 01:17:32.464
image pixel layout,
and then each individual pixel gets

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9285-4
01:17:32.464 --> 01:17:35.067
processed with the fragment processing.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9317-0
01:17:35.467 --> 01:17:42.680
But all these stages had these kind of
streaming array data sets that flowed

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9317-1
01:17:42.680 --> 01:17:47.176
between them.
And it was well suited for having

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9317-2
01:17:47.176 --> 01:17:54.107
dedicated array of processors. Basically,
they all do the same operation.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9329-0
01:17:54.347 --> 01:17:59.050
They just operate on different data and
the different data,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9329-1
01:17:59.050 --> 01:18:02.107
so that's this parallel process called.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9337-0
01:18:04.667 --> 01:18:07.627
Single instruction multiple data or SIMD.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9339-0
01:18:10.987 --> 01:18:11.947
Cindy.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9351-0
01:18:13.027 --> 01:18:17.065
which we'll talk about more single
instruction, multiple data.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9351-1
01:18:17.065 --> 01:18:18.987
So you've got these, you know.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9386-0
01:18:20.547 --> 01:18:25.231
stages and this wasn't even true because
this was before SIMD because SIMD implies

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9386-1
01:18:25.231 --> 01:18:29.802
a certain amount of programming in that
you can give it an instruction and it'll

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9386-2
01:18:29.802 --> 01:18:32.567
know what to do.
These were like fixed function.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9386-3
01:18:32.567 --> 01:18:36.969
They had the instruction was hard-coded
into what they're going to do at each

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9386-4
01:18:36.969 --> 01:18:37.307
stage.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9387-0
01:18:41.147 --> 01:18:41.347
Um...

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9397-0
01:18:43.067 --> 01:18:46.763
So,
but this slowly started to get

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9397-1
01:18:46.763 --> 01:18:48.347
generalized in.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9410-0
01:18:50.267 --> 01:18:54.932
Engineers realize, hey, we wanted to do,
we want to do more interesting things

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9410-1
01:18:54.932 --> 01:18:55.227
with.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9426-0
01:18:56.347 --> 01:19:00.110
We have new ideas on lighting and
materials and things that we can do to

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9426-1
01:19:00.110 --> 01:19:01.707
make our images look more real.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9474-0
01:19:03.467 --> 01:19:08.691
But we don't want to have to like
refabricate new chips and new circuit

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9474-1
01:19:08.691 --> 01:19:14.785
boards every single time we want to make
a change. That's way too slow and tedious.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9474-2
01:19:14.785 --> 01:19:19.500
So they decided, well,
let's introduce some programmability into

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9474-3
01:19:19.500 --> 01:19:22.547
these things. Let's allow people to write.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9513-0
01:19:23.067 --> 01:19:28.755
little snippets of code that will control
certain stages in the pipeline.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9513-1
01:19:28.755 --> 01:19:33.213
And so these initial simple programs were
called shaders,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9513-2
01:19:33.213 --> 01:19:37.210
and they were only allowed in two
different stages,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9513-3
01:19:37.210 --> 01:19:42.667
the vertex processor and the fragment
processor. But for each of those

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9545-0
01:19:43.067 --> 01:19:47.507
stages,
you could write a little shader function

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9545-1
01:19:47.507 --> 01:19:54.575
that would give you some ability to
control the specifics of what was done to

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9545-2
01:19:54.575 --> 01:20:00.827
the vertex stream or to the fragment
stream in this processing flow.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9549-0
01:20:02.347 --> 01:20:05.867
And so all these graphics APIs.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9553-0
01:20:07.707 --> 01:20:09.227
That you've probably heard of.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9554-0
01:20:13.667 --> 01:20:14.187
R.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9574-0
01:20:15.387 --> 01:20:20.807
Basically, extensions of that,
it went from just these two stages to

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9574-1
01:20:20.807 --> 01:20:24.027
basically all stages became programmable.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9576-0
01:20:27.307 --> 01:20:27.707
Um...

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9617-0
01:20:30.187 --> 01:20:36.159
and more and more sophisticated
capabilities and features built in to the

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9617-1
01:20:36.159 --> 01:20:42.775
programmability as game designers wanted
more and more control and ability to put

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9617-2
01:20:42.775 --> 01:20:48.827
physics in their games and, you know,
all kinds of, you know, ray tracing,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9642-0
01:20:49.547 --> 01:20:54.279
details and all kinds of stuff, animation,
action, changing, dynamic changing,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9642-1
01:20:54.279 --> 01:20:59.012
all the stuff that they want in, you know,
the video games that we have today,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/9642-2
01:20:59.012 --> 01:21:01.467
