b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13734-0
02:01:19.347 --> 02:01:21.747
All right, so how does...

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13739-0
02:01:22.707 --> 02:01:25.187
How do GPUs execute in parallel?

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13741-0
02:01:26.227 --> 02:01:26.867
The key.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13792-0
02:01:27.827 --> 02:01:31.553
element is independence.
What is independence?

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13792-1
02:01:31.553 --> 02:01:37.418
So the formal definition in a series or
set of general components S of X,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13792-2
02:01:37.418 --> 02:01:43.680
then you have component S of N has no
dependencies on component S of M for all

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13792-3
02:01:43.680 --> 02:01:45.027
N not equal to M.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13801-0
02:01:45.107 --> 02:01:45.187
The.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13832-0
02:01:47.107 --> 02:01:51.555
Or in other words,
each individual element doesn't depend on

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13832-1
02:01:51.555 --> 02:01:56.147
any of the other elements.
There's a couple different types of

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13832-2
02:01:56.147 --> 02:02:00.522
classes of dependency.
You can have data dependencies where

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13832-3
02:02:00.522 --> 02:02:05.187
components may access or modify the same
resources and maybe...

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13856-0
02:02:05.987 --> 02:02:15.985
reuse them or share this data in a way
that would result in incorrect results if

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13856-1
02:02:15.985 --> 02:02:18.947
the data were not to be.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13861-0
02:02:20.067 --> 02:02:23.107
Correctly handled in the correct order
and sequencing.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13892-0
02:02:24.307 --> 02:02:29.164
Control dependencies are when one
component's events or side effects

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13892-1
02:02:29.164 --> 02:02:33.035
determine if another component will
execute. So again,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13892-2
02:02:33.035 --> 02:02:37.187
if you have these kind of control
dependent codes, then...

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13922-0
02:02:38.387 --> 02:02:43.529
And often it's related to a data
dependency in that, you know,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13922-1
02:02:43.529 --> 02:02:50.384
some route or path is either taken or not
taken depending on the results of another

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13922-2
02:02:50.384 --> 02:02:54.627
and in some cases that dependency can't
be avoided.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13928-0
02:02:56.827 --> 02:02:59.587
But in the case of independent components.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13947-0
02:03:00.507 --> 02:03:03.416
which don't have any of those
dependencies,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13947-1
02:03:03.416 --> 02:03:08.307
then there's no ordering requirements.
They can be computed in any order.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13953-0
02:03:09.267 --> 02:03:12.387
and still get the correct result.
And that's what we need.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13958-0
02:03:13.907 --> 02:03:16.147
So for example, the kind of the...

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13999-0
02:03:18.467 --> 02:03:25.001
The ideal perfect example of completely
independent components is vector addition.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13999-1
02:03:25.001 --> 02:03:29.016
Imagine you have two vectors,
A and B of length N,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13999-2
02:03:29.016 --> 02:03:33.582
and you want to add them.
So this is element wise, right?

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/13999-3
02:03:33.582 --> 02:03:38.147
So basically the sequential or serial
code implementation

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14031-0
02:03:38.547 --> 02:03:43.509
is a for loop for x = 0,
while X is less than N, you just,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14031-1
02:03:43.509 --> 02:03:47.967
for each X,
you compute the value of A of X and B of

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14031-2
02:03:47.967 --> 02:03:54.022
X, and you get your result. Now,
there's no reason you have to do it in

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14031-3
02:03:54.022 --> 02:03:54.947
this order.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14032-0
02:03:55.707 --> 02:03:56.227
Because...

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14041-0
02:03:57.507 --> 02:04:03.347
There's no dependency on C of any other
value.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14047-0
02:04:04.387 --> 02:04:07.267
than the same axes of A and B.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14049-0
02:04:08.147 --> 02:04:08.867
So...

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14054-0
02:04:10.547 --> 02:04:12.707
This is a fundamentally.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14061-0
02:04:14.467 --> 02:04:17.427
Completely independent element-wise
calculation.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14070-0
02:04:20.467 --> 02:04:22.707
and it allows for data parallelism. So.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14117-0
02:04:23.667 --> 02:04:27.218
Basically,
you can imagine that we could do these

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14117-1
02:04:27.218 --> 02:04:30.485
all,
we could compute this whole thing in one

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14117-2
02:04:30.485 --> 02:04:34.746
individual cycle.
If we had an array that could support the

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14117-3
02:04:34.746 --> 02:04:38.652
whole vector A and vector B,
they're both of length N.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14117-4
02:04:38.652 --> 02:04:43.907
We have an adder for each individual 2
inputs, and it produces an output.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14125-0
02:04:44.947 --> 02:04:49.107
for that same element and these could all
be done in one step.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14165-0
02:04:51.587 --> 02:04:56.450
So that's the ideal case. But again,
also there's no ordering.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14165-1
02:04:56.450 --> 02:05:01.853
We could do this backwards.
We could randomly select a value for each

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14165-2
02:05:01.853 --> 02:05:06.407
X as long as we covered N the total
number of N, you know,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14165-3
02:05:06.407 --> 02:05:11.347
values in some order,
we would get the right result at the end.

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14166-0
02:05:14.147 --> 02:05:14.787
So...

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14211-0
02:05:16.307 --> 02:05:20.477
our C serial implementation,
and frequently, and almost always,

b706b327-f0cf-4124-aaba-f498e83a75d2/14211-1
